    "preamble": "Charu Sharma vs The State Of Rajasthan ... on 23 August, 2024 Bench: Manindra Mohan Shrivastava, Madan Gopal Vyas [2024:Rj-Jd:35047-Db] High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur D.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 11321/2021 1. Charu Sharma W/o Shri Himanshu Sharma, Aged About 38 Years, 5-D 35, Sector-5, Maharshi Dayanand Park, Jai Narayan Vyas Colony, Bikaner, District Bikaner (Raj.). 2. Lalit Narayan Purohit S/o Shri Roop Narayan Purohit, Aged About 49 Years, Manawat Purohit Ki Gali, Lalani Vyaso Ka Chowk, Bikaner, District Bikaner (Raj.). ----Petitioners Versus 1. The State Of Rajasthan, Through Its Principal Secretary, Urban Development And Housing Department, Having Office At Food Building, Secretariat, Government Of Rajasthan, Jaipur, 302005. 2. The Petroleum And Explosives Safety Organisation, Through Its Chief Explosive Controller Having Registered Office At A- Block, 5Th Floor, Cgo Complex, Seminary Hills, Nagpur, 440006. 3. Rajasthan State Pollution Control Board, Through Its Chairman Having Registered Office At 4, Jhalana Institutional Area, Jhalana Doongari, Jaipur, Rajasthan 302004 4. Chairman, Urban Improvement Trust, Bikaner Having Office At Rath Khana Colony, Bikaner (Raj.) Pin 334001 5. District Collector And District Magistrate, Bikaner. 6. Mr. Gaurav Gautam S/o Shri Anurag Gautam, 343-A Lane No. 10, Barkat Nagar, Tonk, Dist. Jaipur, Pin 302015. 7. Mr. Rakesh Mordiya S/o Parsaram Mordiya, G-1 Plot No. B-60, University Road, Bapu Nagar, Lal Kothi, Udaipur. ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Ankur Mathur For Respondent(s) : Mr. Ayush Gehlot for Mr. Rajesh Panwar, Charu Sharma vs The State Of Rajasthan ... on 23 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/19329611/ 1 Sr. Advocate-cum- AAG Mr. Ravindra Jala and Mr. Deepak Suthar, AGC for Mr. S.S. Ladrecha, AAG Mr. Chirag Kalani for Mr. B.S. Sandhu for respondent Nos.6 and 7 Mr. S.S. Rathore, AAG (Downloaded on 28/08/2024 at 08:39:03 PM) [2024:RJ-JD:35047-DB] (2 of 3) [CW-11321/2021 ] HON'BLE THE CHIEF JUSTICE MR. MANINDRA MOHAN SHRIVASTAVA HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE MADAN GOPAL VYAS Order 23/08/2024 As per office report, service of notice upon respondent No.7 is received unserved.",
